"{{Term/Store|Tools of the Trade||Series, BotW}}" is a [[Side Quest]] in {{BotW}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Tools of the Trade}}<br/>{{Color BotW|Side Quest|Gerudo Town}}|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

==Overview==
This [[Side Quest]] is one of four that [[Link]] needs to complete as part of "[[The Thunder Helm]]", which will grant him the [[Thunder Helm]]. In [[Gerudo Town]], Link can find [[Isha]] pacing around the market in front of [[Starlight Memories]]. Though she greets Link,<ref>{{Cite|Sav'aaq...|Isha|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Vasaaq...|Isha|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Sav'saaba...|Isha|BotW}}</ref> she remarks that she does not have a reason to be doing so.<ref>{{Cite|Not that I have any reason to be greeting people...|Isha|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link does not speak to Isha until after completing the "[[Divine Beast Vah Naboris (Quest)|Divine Beast Vah Naboris]]" [[Main Quest]], she claims not to have the time to greet people since she is expecting a big rush of customers.<ref>{{Cite|I haven't really got the time to be greeting people, honestly... Now that the Divine Beast has finally calmed down, there should be a rush of customers any second...|Isha|BotW}}</ref> She laments her misfortune ocurring when it did.<ref>{{Cite|So why did something like this have to happen to me now, of all times?|Isha|BotW}}</ref>}}

If Link asks what is wrong, Isha explains that she manages a [[Shop]] specializing in [[Accessory|Accessories]], but she has run out of the [[Flint]] she needs to make them.<ref>{{Cite|[What's the matter?] I manage a shop that specializes in handmade accessories, but I've run out of {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}. I need it to make my items.|Isha|BotW}}</ref> She says that if someone would just give her 10 Flint, she would offer a nice reward.<ref>{{Cite|If only I had {{Color BotW|Red|10}}... Just {{Color BotW|Red|10}}... If some kind vai would give me {{Color BotW|Red|10 pieces of flint}}, I could offer a nice reward...|Isha|BotW}}</ref> However, she realizes that nothing is that easy in the real worlds, and her dreams will change nothing.<ref>{{Cite|I can dream all I want, though... Nothing goes that smoothly in the real world.|Isha|BotW}}</ref>

At Link's inquiry, Isha reveals that she makes her Accessories using [[Gem]]s.<ref>{{Cite|[Accessories?] I use {{Color BotW|Blue|rubies}}, {{Color BotW|Blue|sapphires}}, and other gems to make {{Color BotW|Blue|accessories}}.|Isha|BotW}}</ref> By wearing Gems, one can have their powers transferred to them.<ref>{{Cite|Each gem type has its own power that it can transfer to whoever wears it.|Isha|BotW}}</ref> However, she once again brings up her lack of Flint,<ref>{{Cite|There's nothing I can do about not having any {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}, though...|Isha|BotW}}</ref> which officially begins the Side Quest. Before Link leaves, Isha apologizes for having nothing to give him after visiting.<ref>{{Cite|I'm sorry that you came all the way to see me for nothing.|Isha|BotW}}</ref>

Once Link has 10 pieces of Flint for Isha, he can return to Gerudo Town to give them to her.{{Note|If Link tries to give Isha less than 10 pieces of Flint, she appreciates the gesture, but she claims that she is unable to start without a total of 10 pieces.<ref>{{Cite|Hmm. Well, I do appreciate the gesture... But unless I have {{Color BotW|Red|10 pieces of}} {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}} to get started with, there's no point...|Isha|BotW}}</ref>}} Isha is unsure how to react at first,<ref>{{Cite|[Here's some flint.] Uh...|Isha|BotW}}</ref> but she quickly becomes shocked by Link's generosity.<ref>{{Cite|What?! You're just...giving these to me?|Isha|BotW}}</ref> She thanks him, though she realizes she has to do more to repay him.<ref>{{Cite|Sarqso! But...I can't take this all from you with just a sarqso. We hardly know each other, and you've been so nice...|Isha|BotW}}</ref> However, she does not have any products ready to give to him.<ref>{{Cite|The shop's been closed so long, I hardly have any inventory...|Isha|BotW}}</ref>

Suddenly, Isha realizes she can make an Accessory for Link now that she has Flint.<ref>{{Cite|Oh, of course! Now that I have some {{Color BotW|Blue|flint}}, I could make a jeweled accessory for you if you're interested in something.|Isha|BotW}}</ref> She offers Link a choice between a [[Ruby Circlet]], a [[Sapphire Circlet]], or [[Topaz Earrings]].<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Blue|Rubies}} have the power to grant cold resistance. So you'd like a {{Color BotW|Blue|ruby circlet}}?|Isha|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Blue|Sapphires}} have the power to grant heat resistance. So you think you'd like a {{Color BotW|Blue|sapphire circlet}}?|Isha|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Blue|Topaz}} has the power to grant electric resistance. So you think you'd like {{Color BotW|Blue|topaz earrings}}?|Isha|BotW}}</ref> Whichever one Link chooses, Isha reveals that she had an inkling he might pick it, before stepping away for a moment.<ref>{{Cite|Teehee, I thought you might pick that one. Please give me a moment...|Isha|BotW}}</ref>

Isha presents Link with his new Accessory, noting that it turned out well.<ref>{{Cite|Brand-new, especially for you! I think it turned out really well!|Isha|BotW}}</ref> If he ever needs another Accessory, Isha invites him back to Starlight Memories for a discounted price.<ref>{{Cite|Thanks to you, I got the shop running again, so if you ever need an accessory, please come by for a special discount.|Isha|BotW}}</ref> However, she asks him not to tell any other customers about his special deal.<ref>{{Cite|Just...don't tell my other customers, {{Small|OK?}}|Isha|BotW}}</ref> With this, the Side Quest will be completed.

